{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>For a fire went out.</b> After Heshbon was conquered, and he also waged war against the other towns, which are Ar and Arnon, and conquered them — then it says: ״a fire went out from Heshbon,״ meaning warriors and mighty men, and a flame from that city which is called Kiryat Sichon." "<b>It consumed Ar of Moab.</b> Meaning, from its place fire went out and consumed them — like ״ותצא אש מאבימלך ותאכל את אנשי שכם״ and ״ומבעלי שכם ותאכל את אבימלך״ — meaning from them and through them. And this is the parable that they made about the might of Sichon, to inform you how great was the power of Moses, that he defeated and killed him. And likewise they made a parable about the children of Ammon: ״הלא את אשר יורישך כמוש אלהיך״."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:55.055522207Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}